{"name":"VIC 20 Pink","hex":"#ea9ff6","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"vic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Virgin Islands Creole."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A victim of a homicide."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vic"},{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"VIC-20","blocks":[{"text":"The VIC-20 is an 8-bit entry level home computer that was sold by Commodore Business Machines. The VIC-20 was announced in September 1980, roughly three years after Commodore's first personal computer, the PET. The VIC-20 was the first computer of any description to sell one million units, and sales of the VIC-20 eventually reached 2.5 million units."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Commodore-VIC-20-FL.jpg/330px-Commodore-VIC-20-FL.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/VIC-20"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/VIC-20_Display.jpg/500px-VIC-20_Display.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaig